{
  "comment": "Import mapping for Michael Willis's Tchimera Drum Kit (github.com/michaelwillis/tchimera-drum-kit), an SFZ kit built from Vincent 'Tchackpoum' Sermone's ReaperDrummer recordings: a Premier kick, a Supraphonic-style snare and the Ludwig Black Cortex toms, hi-hat and cymbals. full_kit.sfz plays five outputs: kick, snare, toms and hi-hat close mics (mono) and a stereo overhead pair (samples/overheads and samples/cymbals; the cymbals have no close mics). Overheads and SFZ pans are from the drummer's seat, so the overheads are swapped and the close-mic pans are the SFZ's, mirrored. The SFZ balances each drum's close mic against the overheads with master/global volumes (kick 15/18 dB, snare 10/18, toms 6,4,6,3/3, hi-hat 10/0). The format has one level per zone for every mic of a hit (the importer averages them), so each close mic carries the difference (close - overheads) and the piece takes back half of it ((overheads - close) / 2): both mics then play at the SFZ's levels. The hi-hat's four openness steps are read at CC4 values inside each step's range (CC4 127 = closed); edge steps carry openness/stroke because their ids aren't standard ones. Tom 'rim' keys play head-edge hits (about 5 dB quieter than centre hits, not rimshots), so they're imported as 'edge' and follow positional sensing. The grabbed-cymbal copies (lopolyaft) and release triggers aren't imported; grabs choke by aftertouch.",
  "format": "sfz",
  "matches": [
    "tchimera-drum-kit-master",
    "tchimera-drum-kit",
    "Tchimera",
    "hihat_open_4_bow.sfz"
